# Nava workflow

- A parent-workspace `nava-workflow.mdc` may be older. Where its process or routing rules differ, use this worktree’s rules and `AGENTS.md`.
- Choose planning and execution skills for the task, risk and owner direction. Honor explicitly requested skills.
- For nontrivial work, inspect relevant code/config and consult documented solutions when useful.
- Choose plan, design and DevEx reviews in proportion to scope and risk. Do not require multiple review rituals by default.
- Use test-driven or subagent-driven development when appropriate or explicitly requested. Never discard existing code merely because tests came later. Preserve project-required same-head review and fresh verification.
- `ponytail` persistent mode stays off unless explicitly invoked. `ponytail-review` remains review-only.
- Document verified, reusable learnings when useful or requested; do not require a document for every task.
- Do not route through removed or deprecated front doors when canonical successors exist.
- Pilot-RDS safety rule overrides every skill, plan, autonomy mandate, and test instruction.
